    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate leaning heavily on **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Corbin Carroll** as our primary engines of production. **Tyler Soderstrom** leads the roster with a 72.71 score, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Freddy Peralta; the combination of a 10% park boost and the hitter-friendly spot at the #2 hole makes him our premier start. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** remains an essential cornerstone, with his 72.46 score driven by his dual-threat potential against Hughes. Despite a moderate xERA from the opposition, **Corbin Carroll**\u2019s elite speed profile allows us to prioritize him even when matchups are less than ideal, though today\u2019s setup remains firmly in his favor. \n\nWe are also capitalizing on situational edges elsewhere in the lineup. **Mickey Moniak** presents an intriguing play with a 61.62 score, buoyed by a significant 14% platoon adjustment against Soroka, which elevates him above several higher-projected bats. Similarly, **Isaac Paredes** (60.10) catches a notable tailwind boost that, when combined with his projected #3 lineup spot, makes him a lock for our active roster. Conversely, the decision to slot **Austin Riley** in the UTIL spot was the tightest call of the morning; his 49.87 score sits squarely in the marginal tier, further dampened by a 37% rain risk that necessitates close monitoring. While bench stalwarts like **Jose Caballero** and **Josh Naylor** are unavailable due to team off-days, the roster remains deep with high-upside prospects like **Travis Bazzana** and **Edwin Arroyo** waiting for their next window to contribute to our stolen base objectives. We are currently navigating the absences of **James Wood** and **Trevor Story** on the IL, but with **Gabriel Moreno** providing consistent value in the #3 hole, we have sufficient coverage to weather today's volatility.",
